00:05:15,140 --> 00:05:19,860
Here's a tip. Light therapy is not black and white, where one size fits all.

00:05:20,660 --> 00:05:26,340
So when we ask about things such as dosing, which is the duration and intensity of the light used,

00:05:26,340 --> 00:05:33,700
the normal answer is it depends. There are several factors to consider when determining the dosing

00:05:33,700 --> 00:05:39,220
for your treatment. These include the age of the injury or condition, the age and overall health of

00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:46,660
the patient, the size of the injury, medications being taken, and the response from the patient throughout

00:05:46,660 --> 00:05:53,860
the treatment. All of these aspects factor into the delivery of light. So when we offer suggestions

00:05:53,860 --> 00:05:59,540
for time and intensity, please keep in mind that these are starting settings and you may need to modify

00:05:59,540 --> 00:06:06,660
them based on your results. In general, if a patient is new to light therapy, it's always best to go slow.

00:06:06,980 --> 00:06:11,860
Thank you for watching. I'm Sharon and I appreciate your time and I wish you

00:06:11,860 --> 00:06:13,860
